 knew what my heart said i  should do and i should give it away to  my niece i'll be honest in my brain i  thought what if i need it what if there  was a situation and i need a backup  computer and  i just had to kind of smack myself in  the face and say yes if i keep it i'm  maybe going to use it in the future in a  few years  in some sort of scenario likely never  but if i give it away  i know that it's going to be used it's  going to make a greater impact it's  going to be so helpful for her i so i  thought about all those options and and  so i am going to be giving it away  and along with that i had a mouse which  i realized i had not been using i  actually had this boxed up and i didn't  realize it until i decided that i was  going to give away the computer so it's  a perfectly usable mouse but for me i  actually even edit on photoshop with  just  you know my little  what do you call that thing the pad on  the computer i don't use the mouse and  so there's no need for that either so  this eliminates two items in one the  next item is one that i'm actually going  to be selling and it's my tony llama  cowgirl boots and i've actually had  these for  over five years now but i've worn them  about four or five times and i realized  that it was time to let these go because  i need some winter boots where i live it  actually gets below freezing and i  needed some boots but i could not  justify having a new pair of boots when  i have one pair of boots that i never  wear and so i decided i'm going to be  selling these i'll maybe get like five  or ten dollars for them but you know  what the money has already been spent  really the damage has been done i'm not  going to be getting that money back and  so for me i need to eliminate one and  just acknowledge that i already spent  the money it's done it's not coming back  and  just move on with the pair that i do  really like and enjoy and will wear so  in a way it's kind of eliminating the  guilt because when i see them i feel  guilty that i spent the money on them  and that i don't wear them the next item  is a handmade shawl and this one is  truly very very special to me and it's  kind of hard to get rid of so story with  this is my aunt and grandma in mexico  make handmade shawls and it takes them  hours to do they sell them in mexico for  dirt cheap i mean it is sad the amount  of money that they get paid for these  and so  what i did um and my mom did the last  time that she visited to mexico is we  bought several of them from them so that  they could kind of make some money and  we maybe could either keep them or sell  them my mom would sell them and i would  just hoard them because i didn't want to  get rid of them to me they were so  special they were made by hands  of people that i love and i just  couldn't let them go uh and then i  realized i have these beautiful items  that are  well made that some people love and  could use instead of keeping them boxed  up what would my grandma and my aunt  want would they want for these items to  be boxed up and locked away for nobody  to use or would they want people to  actually use them and love them and  enjoy them and so i thought of an  individual who is very classy she loves  handmade things and i decided to give  this to her so that she could make use  of it because really it was collecting  dust in my closet and i just did not  think that that was fair for an item  that i value and i think is very special  and beautiful sometimes i think that it  can be hard to get rid of an item if it  does bring that emotional value to me  those items do bring an emotional value  but i also think of it as  what would  this person want of that item would they  want this item to be boxed up or would  they want this item to be used and loved  and enjoyed okay next up is kind of a a  simple one it's sweatpants my husband  basically bought a new pair of  sweatpants and so we just didn't really  need an extra pair he had one that he  rarely ever wore and so this one is  going to be chunked away to donation  pile it's soft it's in good condition  but it was rarely used time to go the  next item is actually one that i'm kind  of embarrassed that i'm admitting to but  it's a table runner and placemats so to  give you the story this table that is  behind me was made by my husband he took  several days to make it because i really  wanted a farmhouse live edge table i  drew out the parameters of what i wanted  it to look like and he made it just the  way that i wanted it and then there i  went putting a table runner and  placemats on it to hide its beauty i  feel like basically i took this  beautiful piece of art and i slapped a  sticker on it to hide all of the beauty  that it provided which is kind of sad  and he never told me anything about it  but now i realize what what was i  thinking so i now decided i'm going to  be removing that we're just going to be  appreciating the natural beauty of  this art piece it's an art piece i want  to appreciate all of its imperfections  all of the grooves all of the little  holes and  little lines on them how smooth it is  and appreciate the meaning behind the  work that it took  and what it really means to us versus  just  an item that could be purchased from a  store to decorate something the next  item is rather a simple one and it's  napkin holders and i'm excited about  getting rid of it because it's one less  thing off this table so we can better  showcase its beauty but also we hadn't  gotten rid of these napkin holders  because we had had packs of disposable  napkins and i have over the years been  trying to purchase less and less  disposable items and purchase more  reusable however because we already had  these packs of disposable napkins i saw  it this way we have already purchased  them the damage has already been done to  the environment i can't just like put  them back in the tree they've already  been made and so i decided that we were  going to use them up until they were  finished and then we would go and buy  reusable napkins and so now we have  purchased some reusable napkins once  these disposable ones run out we will  use reusable from now on instead of  disposables and now we won't need the  napkin holders next up is this stack of  vcrs so i had some vcrs that we don't  have the ability to play because we  don't even have a vcr player however i  realized that there are places that can  transfer these videos into dvd format so  certain places like walmart cvs  walgreens can actually transfer this for  a cost however if you don't want to  actually pay for these items sometimes  you can look at purchasing these items  on dvd format so some of the old vcr  movies that we had had when we were kids  that i loved actually now have been made  in dvd format but for those special  movies like maybe you have home movies  that you just really don't want to get  rid of look into transferring them from  bcr into dvd next up is some kids  clothes so basically with kids they  outgrow their clothes so quickly and  what we do with the gently used clothes  is we take them to a consignment shop  that gives us a tiny amount of money for  it however i can use this amount of  money to purchase new items so i can  basically take the old items that no  longer fit them sell those for a small  amount of money but use that towards  purchasing new items that do fit them  that they can grow into and i'm also a  big fan of this because i feel like this  reduces waste this is one less item  that's produced new and i'm buying  something that is used so not only is it  better for the wallet but it's better  for the environment as well the next  item is some non-fitting shirts and this  one is something that i kind of had to  give myself permission on so here  recently i have now weaned my child from  breastfeeding and any woman who has ever  breastfed a child been pregnant or even  if you haven't hormones and things can  fluctuate and our weight can fluctuate  and you know what sometimes we need to  give ourselves permission  to have the items that make us feel good  and look good and not just have this  item to remind us that we need to get to  that weight or get to that way that we  were before i think that it's important  for us to realize that we should accept  ourselves who we are now and have the  clothes that make us feel good so for me  i'm eliminating these they no longer fit  me  the bosoms are not what they used to be  that's okay the next item is kind of a  sentimental item for me it's harder for  me than it is for my daughter and this  is stuffed kids toys our daughter has  autism and she plays with toys  differently where another child may play  house and play dress up and those sorts  of things she likes to line things up  and that is perfectly okay  you know i didn't realize  with her that this was autism that we  were seeing and i tried to really force  on her well let's play this and let's  play that and and i've now come to  realize that it's okay  so with me getting rid of some of these  toys that she has never played with it's  not getting rid of this ideal of what i  had of parenting and childhood would be  for her  rather it's me telling grown up anna i  love you just the way you are you don't  have to be anyone else but you and if  you don't want to play this way then  that's okay i accept you just as you are  and so you can see that getting rid of  an item can be so much more than just  getting rid of a physical item  it's really what ties what emotional  ties the item has is it providing guilt  does it make you feel like you need to  be a certain way be a certain person and  so i just kind of encourage you to look  at your items there may be certain items  that are really sentimental and  difficult for you to get rid of and just  kind of evaluate the why is it because  it reminds you of a past relationship  and you don't want to let it go  or is it something that really provides  you joy or is it because it was an item  that belonged to your deceased  grandmother and it's really difficult  for you to let that go just really  evaluate the emotions behind it because  a lot of the items that we have have a  lot of emotional ties and it can be very  difficult to get rid of these items i  feel like i've included a lot of  sentimental items and then i just throw  in some random ones like this basket so  we have had uh this basket for a while  and i've i've had it in the closet as a  maybe donating item but i've kept it  just in case because you know just in  case may happen and i think that with  storage items that can really happen a  lot so we have these storage items and  we want to just fill them up and so i  realized that if i'm not using storage  items all the better because if i have  storage items that aren't being used i'm  going to find some items to put inside  them so that just kind of makes more  clutter so you know what  goodbye storage basket next up is some  non-used puzzles so if you have any  puzzles that are maybe like missing  pieces or just puzzles that are not  really used in general analyze what  kinds of puzzles you actually use what  kinds of games you are enjoying and what  items have a little too much dust that  maybe haven't been pulled out in a while  because perhaps it's time to let them go  next up is a wine bottle opener okay  this one's not really that big of a deal  it's a tiny little item but we realized  that we don't really drink wine we have  had a wine bottle that was gifted to us  months ago and we still have yet to open  it and it's actually not even one that  has the cork it's just the screw on and  so if we're not really purchasing wine  we're not really drinking wine on a  regular basis like maybe once a year why  do we even have a wine bottle opener and  lastly an umbrella so i had asked you  guys in a previous video if you  recommended that i keep or declutter an  umbrella because we don't use an  umbrella we go outside and if it rains  we just get rained on and we embrace  that and we just have learned to just  enjoy that and be okay with that so  we're actually going to be parting ways  with the umbrella i don't think that we  need to have one more item if it's not  being used and it could certainly be  used by somebody else so sometimes i  think just look at your items and see if  you're not using them maybe think of  somebody that can use them sometimes  that helps me when i'm not sure if i  should get rid of an item if i have  someone in mind that i know can use it  and love it then that really eases my  guilt and makes it a lot easier to get  rid of so hopefully this list has been  enjoyable it's been helpful but if so  please give it a thumbs up i would love  to hear your comments as well though  what items are you thinking of  decluttering what ways are you going to  be clearing your space in your home and  making room for the things that you love  i thank you so much for watching and i  can't wait to hear from you until next  time bye  [Music]

